    <!-- Date Changes -->
    <section class="content-section" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2>Why NDT to EST Conversion Can Change the Date</h2>
      <p>
        Because NDT is 2.5 hours ahead of EST, early morning hours in Newfoundland (between 00:00 and 02:29 AM) correspond to late evening on the previous calendar day in EST.
      </p>
      <h3>Date Rollover Window</h3>
      <ul style="padding-left: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.9;">
        <li><strong>NDT 00:00 to 02:29 AM</strong> → EST 9:30 PM to 11:59 PM → <strong>Previous calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>NDT 02:30 AM</strong> → EST 00:00 (Midnight) → <strong>Same calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>NDT 06:00 AM</strong> → EST 03:30 AM → <strong>Same calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>NDT 12:00 PM (Noon)</strong> → EST 09:30 AM → <strong>Same calendar day</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Always check both the <strong>time and date</strong> when communicating across Newfoundland and Eastern Time. Our converter updates calendar dates automatically.
      </p>
    </section>

