          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">NDT times between 00:00 and 02:29 AM belong to the previous calendar day in EST. Always verify the date.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing NDT with NST</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">NDT is UTC-2:30 (summer daylight saving). NST is UTC-3:30 (winter standard). Ensure you are converting the active seasonal offset.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing EST with EDT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">EST is UTC-5 (winter). EDT is UTC-4 (summer). During summer, NDT is 1.5 hours ahead of EDT.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
